    "created_at": "2026-06-23T17:24:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-23T17:24:33Z",
    "body": "I can't find any evidence in chromium that visibility:collapse for the hidden attribute was ever implemented, and we are just setting display:none on those elements right now.\n\nIs there anything else in the HTML spec which shows that display:none should not be used on those tables elements when they have the hidden attribute? It certainly seems like it was always broken.\n\nIt also looks like the usage of visibility:collapse was added to the spec several years before visibility:collapse was even implemented in chromium.\n\nProbably we should change the selector to avoid all those tables elements like this?\n```css\n[hidden]:not([hidden=until-found i]):not(embed):not(colgroup):not(col):not(thead):not(tbody):not(tfoot):not(tr) {\n  display: none;\n}\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
